Functions in Sql

=>Aggregate Function:
THis function is used to perform calculation on a set of values and return a single value.
Examples
avg,max,min,count,sum 
1-Count
select count(*) from users;
or
select count(*) from users where gender="Male";

2- min salary & max salary
select Min(salary) as min_salary , Max(salary) as max_salary from users;

3-sum
select sum(salary) as total from users;

4-Group by & avg

The group by statement is used with aggregate functions to group the result-set by one or more columns.
We can select only those columns which were present in group by command.
We can use only those columns in group by which data is repitative

Every column in your SELECT that is NOT inside an aggregate function (COUNT, AVG, SUM, MAX, MIN) MUST be in GROUP BY
select gender , avg(salary) as gender_salary from users group by gender;

String Function
1-lower & length
select id,gender ,lower(name) as lower,length(name) as namelength from users;

2-concat
select id,gender ,lower(name) as lower,concat(lower(name),"787") as username from users;

3-Current time & current year,month
select id,gender ,now() as time, year(date_of_birth) as yob,month(date_of_birth) as month from users;

4-datediff
select name ,datediff(curDate(),date_of_birth) as days from users;
