Union & Union all
=>2 aisy tables jin ka apas me koi relation ni ha un dono table ki kisi  b same column name field k data ko merge krny ko union kehty ha.
In case of union, duplicates will be ignore  (see below example ,agr users me tayyab ha aur admin me b tayyab ha,tu ye admin k tayyab ko ignore kr dy gi)
select name from users union  select name from admin_users;

=>Union all:
If we want duplication remove na hu,then use union all,ab tayyab 2 dfa show hu ga
select name from users union all select name from admin_users;

also we can add extra column for their identity
select name,"Normal User" as role from users union  select name,"Admin User" as role from admin_users;//role will be added as separate column

=>Ordered by
also we can get the data of those first which have higher salary 
select name,"Normal User" as role,salary  from users union  select name,"Admin User" as role,salary from admin_users order by salary desc;

Rules of UNION
The number of columns and their data types must match in all SELECT statements.(means users mei mainy srf name select kiya but admin_users me mainy name,email dono likhy,that is not allowed in union,users mei b email likhna pary ga)
UNION removes duplicates by default.
UNION ALL keeps duplicates.



