                                                    "SUB QUERY IN FROM"
                                                    
 eXAMPLE 1:
    we need to have total score student has earned and number of exams he has attempted ,also we have to show student name and student branch in result.
    
    Solution:
    Without subquery:
    I tried to do it first by my own without subquery and it works,see below
    
     select a.name,a.branch,sum(b.score) as total_score,count(b.student_id) as total_attempted,b.student_id from students as a inner join exam_scores as b on a.student_id=b.student_id group by b.student_id order by total_score desc;

    With SubQuery:
    select std.name,std.branch,total_stats.total_score,total_stats.totalattempted,std.student_id from (
select sum(score) as total_score,count(student_id) as totalattempted,student_id from exam_scores group by student_id
) as total_stats inner join students as std on std.student_id=total_stats.student_id;


Example 2:
    For each project get student name,branch and project obtained marks and also their average exam score on same row.
    
    Solution 1 :
select project_marks.name,project_marks.branch,project_marks.marks as project_marks_gained,ex_score.student_id,avg(ex_score.score) as average_exam_marks  
from (
  select a.name,a.branch,b.marks,a.student_id from students as a inner join projects as b on a.student_id =b.student_id
  ) as project_marks 
  inner join exam_scores as ex_score 
  on ex_score.student_id=project_marks.student_id 
  group by project_marks.student_id,project_marks.name,project_marks.branch,project_marks_gained order by average_exam_marks desc;
  
  
  Solution 2: recommended
  select s.name,s.branch,p.marks,avg_marks.avg_score from students as s 
  inner join projects as p on s.student_id=p.student_id 
 inner join ( select student_id,avg(score) as avg_score from exam_scores group by student_id) as avg_marks 
  on p.student_id=avg_marks.student_id;

